    "summary": "Twelve-year-old Mohammed Zaid prepares to move from Hyderabad to Dubai, leaving his friend Salman an old wheat one-rupee coin treasure and asking him to fly their torn blue kite at 5:30 each evening.",
    "text": "Salman,\nEveryone is saying we are moving to Dubai because Abbu got a job. I am happy and also not happy, like when you eat a mango that is half sweet and half sour.\nI want you to have my one-rupee coin, the old one with the picture of the wheat. Remember when we found it behind the temple wall and decided it was a pirate treasure? You said we should never spend it. Good. I have not.\nI also leave you our kite, the blue one with the torn tail. We never cut anyone's string with it, but it flew higher than all the expensive ones, and that counts.\nPlease keep going to the terrace every evening at 5:30. Even if I am not there, fly something. I will look up from Dubai and tell myself, that is Salman's kite, that blue dot. Maybe it is not really yours, maybe it is just a pigeon. But I will pretend.\nYour best friend forever, even if the net is slow, Zaid"
